  "body": "Release 0.16.0 (minor; major is 0, so the breaking change bumps minor).\n\nBREAKING: project files move from v57 to v58 (PR #381, optional tool holder body). Builds before 0.16.0 refuse v58 files; 0.15.0 files open and are migrated on save. Also stricter posts: Tormach and Siemens 840D refuse machines without `safe_retract`; a probing post needs `onProbeGuard`.\n\nHeadlines: fixtures judged against their real mesh, tools with modelled holder bodies (mill and lathe), one NC file per mount, Machines pane editing, a much larger MCP surface, orthographic projection, Apache-2.0 relicense, and a long run of sim and gouge-gate fixes. Full text in RELEASE_NOTES.md; 54 rows added to CHANGELOG.md; 56 decision files gathered into RECOMMENDED.md.\n\nGate: `scripts/release.ps1 -Version 0.16.0 -NoTag -Installer` ran the full release tier on this tree, green (638 test binaries ok, 0 failed), release build OK, post.exe reports 0.16.0.\n\nArtifact: dist/camcraft-0.16.0-win-x64.zip (unsigned: no certificate configured; no installer: Inno Setup ISCC.exe not found on this machine). No tag; tag main after merge.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
